---
description: Tag React components for component-details-overlay so each shows its name on the live page
globs: "**/*.tsx"
alwaysApply: false
---

This project uses `component-details-overlay`. When you create a React component, add `{...tag('ComponentName')}` to its outermost DOM element.

```tsx
import { tag } from 'component-details-overlay';

export function Card({ children }) {
  return <section {...tag('Card')} className="card">{children}</section>;
}
```

- The name matches the component's own name, in PascalCase.
- Put the tag before any `...rest` spread so callers can still override it.
- In a Next.js Server Component, import `tag` from `component-details-overlay/tag`.
- A component that only renders another tagged component and adds no element of its own doesn't need a tag.
- To set the overlay up in a project that doesn't have it yet, read `node_modules/component-details-overlay/AI-SETUP.md`.
